        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 653,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 311,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "If the local water depth is relatively small most waves of practical interest have become shallow water waves. From a numerical point of view the smallest wave that can be represented on the grid has a wavelength of. If we define a shallow water wave as a wave for which  then the smallest wave has become a shallow water wave when the depth is:"
