        "start_xml_ordinal": 16961,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 655,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 313,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "If  then it appears appropriate to disable the calculation of the non-hydrostatic pressure by removing the point from the linear system in a similar way as for a dry point. Removing these points might improve the convergence rate and stability of the pressure correction algorithm. Presently it appears that for low values of  there is hardly any difference in simulations without the removal of these points. For this reason the default value of  is set to zero, which practically means that points are never removed for this reason."
